From 098a6dfd38d68b0cfab606a09a2e09fa7716893d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Will Eaton <weaton@redhat.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 12:26:39 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] feat(cuinterpose): expose the coordinator as a library

Move peer validation and the inspect, prepare and restore phases into
cuinterpose_coordinator's lib target. The binary keeps its arguments and
behaviour and calls the library.

Peer::new takes any path that reaches a participant's control socket, so a
node agent can drive the phases in-process, for example through
/proc/PID/root/tmp/cuinterpose-N.sock, instead of executing the coordinator
inside the workload's mount namespace. inspect returns the validated records
so a caller can decide whether any memory is shared before it prepares.
